  { title: 'Half-reactions', narration: 'Click each electrode: the anode oxidizes chloride (2Cl⁻ → Cl₂ + 2e⁻) and the cathode reduces sodium ions (Na⁺ + e⁻ → Na). Together they sum to 2NaCl(l) → 2Na(l) + Cl₂(g).' }
];
